{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing","id":918701,"title":"Rules: Vampire the Requiem (Second Edition) Protean vs. Clothing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-21T11:01:58-07:00","id":918701,"title":"Rules: Vampire the Requiem (Second Edition) Protean vs. Clothing","content":"I've scoured the book and can't find anything, not even a fluff piece describing the effects of Protean related to clothing. There's an old post from 2013 that predates 2.0 that doesn't really have a definitive answer. I've consulted with 3 different storytellers and had 3 different answers. One says Protean only relates to Flesh as it only mentions flesh. Another says &quot;of course the simple clothes change with you&quot;, and a third says &quot;depending on the theme of the game, I'd rule it either way, as the story needed it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like without any definitive line relating to clothes being in the book. All of these answers are correct. There's no mention in the FAQ even related to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Clarification? Official Ruling from on High?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T11:52:41-07:00","id":918721,"title":"","content":"The simple changes don't seem to matter for clothing much. the more advanced changes though... well, do you want to deal with naked vampires running around after changing into animal or mist form? If you think complications would add to the story, pick that model. Otherwise just handwave it away.<br /> <br /> Note: Werewolves used to have this problem and needed a Rite to get around it. But that became so common it was laughable, and has now been incorporated into Harmony. So ask yourself - does a high Protean vampire possess the same personal control as a Werewolf in tune with their spirit side?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-21-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:47:35-07:00","id":918752,"title":"","content":"I'm with ya. In 1.0 it clearly stated in the first blurb for Protean that Clothes changed with you. <br /> <br /> And now, even the most basic Cub in Wolf 2.0 can shift with their clothes.<br /> <br /> Yet the description seems entirely missing one way or the other for Protean in 2.0.<br /> <br /> And unless otherwise specified, whatever you go with would be for all things: Level 1 earthmelding, level 5 mist form. I agree that it depends on the change for levels 2 and 4 as to whether you'd shred something or otherwise have an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:46:03-07:00","id":918809,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that in 2e, Protean 1 is already an ability to meld with materials. It could be assumed, by the fact Disciplines now build on each other more clearly, that this is what gives you the power to meld with/transform alongside your clothes too at Protean 2+ and up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:58:08-07:00","id":918817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918809#post918809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point out that in 2e, Protean 1 is already an ability to meld with materials. It could be assumed, by the fact Disciplines now build on each other more clearly, that this is what gives you the power to meld with/transform alongside your clothes too at Protean 2+ and up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly... fantastic reply, certainly not an aspect I'd considered. <br /> <br /> With that in mind Saibot, purely for discussion purposes, what would you say then is the effect of wearing Plate Armor or Reinforced clothing/armor? Increased Blood cost to meld/shapeshift with those worn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:07:35-07:00","id":918826,"title":"","content":"Naked and Afraid would make an entertaining Persistent Condition for shifters in general with this sort of problem<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 06-21-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:07:37-07:00","id":918827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrimsonOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918817#post918817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firstly... fantastic reply, certainly not an aspect I'd considered.<br /> <br /> With that in mind Saibot, purely for discussion purposes, what would you say then is the effect of wearing Plate Armor or Reinforced clothing/armor? Increased Blood cost to meld/shapeshift with those worn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I think that is mainly an ST call on whether they want to penalise this particular strategy or not. Certainly there is some sense behind it and adding 1 or 2 Vitae to the cost would not be asking too much for the chance of a fully armoured almost unpreventable ambush (for example).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:57:55-07:00","id":918839,"title":"","content":"I wanted to add my opinion to the mix of things. I understand that there are other interpretations to this power, but I will give you my reasoning.<br /> <br /> The first dot of protean states that the earth opens up and you sink into it. You are cocooned inside the ground. You have to pay extra to sink into anything else based on it's durability. Concrete for example. So I am torn on that one. I think you could take your clothes because it seems more like the ground eats you...<br /> <br /> dots 2,3,4 all specifically state that the vampire's flesh changes. Meaning Body, skin and bones. These are inward out changes. The beast inside of you trying to get out. Which seems to imply to me that should you turn into a kitten.. you would be in a pool of clothes or if you turn into a tiger, your clothes would shred. Because they are not part of your flesh. I believe that if it was intended to be otherwise they would have said &quot;body&quot; &quot;person&quot; or any other word that has a different connotation . <br /> <br /> 5th you burst into smoke. it even says that the pinnacle of protean you become &quot;Nothing more than smoke and hunger&quot; not &quot;nothing more than smoke, hunger and your wallet&quot; (ok being a little silly here )<br /> <br /> I can see the other points that Wolves can now change with clothes, but that's only if their self control is on par. Their harmony is right. Protean isnt about control, its about giving in to the beast. The primal part of you<br /> <br /> <br /> I dont want to take what Saibot said out of context, but I dont think &quot; <i>Protean 1 is already an ability to meld with materials</i> &quot; . I mean at least that is not what protean is intended for. It's not meant to be a power that lets you merge with materials. In saying so, to me, Creates a slippery slope. It makes me ask, why cant I merge into the wall of the bank vault and come out the other side? Why cant I merge into the second story floor and hide? Protean is an ability that brings you closer to the beast inside. The animal. Nature. It is very bestial. And beasts don't care about clothing or how inconvenient it is to have no clothes on hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T16:22:15-07:00","id":918844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918721#post918721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simple changes don't seem to matter for clothing much. the more advanced changes though... well, do you want to deal with naked vampires running around after changing into animal or mist form? If you think complications would add to the story, pick that model. Otherwise just handwave it away.<br /> <br /> Note: Werewolves used to have this problem and needed a Rite to get around it. But that became so common it was laughable, and has now been incorporated into Harmony. So ask yourself - does a high Protean vampire possess the same personal control as a Werewolf in tune with their spirit side?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think an interesting ruling would be borrow inspiration from Werewolf, and have clothing tied to the identity of the Man (as opposed to the Beast) and have mid-to-high Humanity character's clothing shift with them because they more fully identify with clothed humanity (lower case 'h'), while inversely as the Beast's influence rises within a vampire they lose that ability and are reduced to a wild-eyed naked dirt-caked predatory corpse-creature. This does two things. it reinforces low vs high humanity stereo types of savagery, and also make maintaining Humanity more rewarding, which is good because it can cost Experience to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-21-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T16:51:27-07:00","id":918851,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the &quot;your shapeshifting has left you naked! What ever will you do?&quot; scene is only fun a couple of times. After a while it's just tedious and getting in the way of the rest of the game. Therefore, Protean shifts clothes with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:17:47-07:00","id":918870,"title":"","content":"Part of the point being made is that running around without your clothes isn't a very human thing to do, and might be more appropriate for a low Humanity vampire, who in turn wouldn't be bothered by a lack of clothing. Many of the stranger older vampires in the books don't seem to wear clothes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:24:22-07:00","id":918875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918851#post918851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the &quot;your shapeshifting has left you naked! What ever will you do?&quot; scene is only fun a couple of times. After a while it's just tedious and getting in the way of the rest of the game. Therefore, Protean shifts clothes with you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Erm.. I dont think the rules and powers as written and the tediousness of scenes go together. Sometimes feeding scenes get tedious or the &quot;you once again have woken up with not enough vitae and are probably going to frenzy again&quot; therefore should we not feed? <br /> <br /> If you know you are going to shapeshift.. Carry around a backpack or have pockets where you have stashed stuff around the city. Have your friends carry shit for you or collect your clothes. Have a back up plan. Prepare. My current Daeva has protean and I havent run into any issues whatsoever yet with my protean leaving me naked...<br /> <br /> Again though, that's just me.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the arguments where you take evidence from the Wolf game and Evidence from vampire to compare. I do like the humanity comparison and reward for staying in that higher range. It's an interesting concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:31:30-07:00","id":918878,"title":"","content":"Not sure how it happened... double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:41:47-07:00","id":918882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918875#post918875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm.. I dont think the rules and powers as written and the tediousness of scenes go together. Sometimes feeding scenes get tedious or the &quot;you once again have woken up with not enough vitae and are probably going to frenzy again&quot; therefore should we not feed?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your group doesn't like feeding scenes and finds them boring? Yeah, honestly. Just make feeding rolls and handwave the actual scene if you don't think playing it out will be fun. Personally, I'd wonder what appeals to your group about vampire if not interested in feeding, as that to me is a central part of the drama of being a vampire. But, I'm not one to judge, if that's what your group enjoys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=918875#post918875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know you are going to shapeshift.. Carry around a backpack or have pockets where you have stashed stuff around the city. Have your friends carry shit for you or collect your clothes. Have a back up plan. Prepare. My current Daeva has protean and I havent run into any issues whatsoever yet with my protean leaving me naked...<br /> <br /> Again though, that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine too if you find that fun. Wouldn't be to my taste, but if it's to yours, rock on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T19:36:38-07:00","id":918913,"title":"","content":"So, is the takeaway from this discussion really that there isn't a hard and fast ruling on the field?<br /> <br /> To me the feeling I get is that it's really up to the THEME of the game. And just because a house rule for one game in this case works, doesn't mean it would apply to the next game a group runs.<br /> <br /> If you want to be the flashy swarm of bats that reforms as your awesome self clad in Roman armor, and it fits the theme of the game, go with it. <br /> <br /> If you are playing a game that logistically speaking, you need to have a 'plan' (That's asking a lot some times), then play a game that makes your player use the space between their ears and come up with a solution together.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, one thing Vitalis and I discussed on the side was a Merit/Devotion requiring perhaps Vigor or Resilience to end the discussion altogether. If that fits your game, do that!<br /> <br /> For me, the initial choice was simple: The ST said I'm naked, so, I was naked. The scene continued and made for some certainly interesting storytelling. But it also sparked a curiosity to scour the book and do a lot of research to try and find it covered. <br /> <br /> First Edition very clearly spelled out that Protean changes included your clothing, but I say that with the firm understanding that 1.0 and 2.0 are not the same game/powers. <br /> <br /> I'd like to thank anyone who's contributed so far, and anyone who continues to chime in on the discussion, it's great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T21:07:10-07:00","id":918934,"title":"","content":"ST call, which is why it's not stated.<br /> <br /> Use Humanity as a guideline: less than 4 Humanity, clothes don't change because the Beast rejects the Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T07:51:42-07:00","id":919088,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that it actually does not make a difference whether Protean 1 allows you to literally fuse with the material or just command it to allow you entrance and cocoon yourself in it. Both show that Protean has some degree of mastery over inert matter, which could then be applied to clothes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:03:55-07:00","id":919090,"title":"","content":"Of course Protean 1 melds you into the ground. It's a <i>shapeshifting</i> power, not a dirt-control power. Having the first dot not involve shapeshifting would render the whole discipline nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T04:41:34-07:00","id":919644,"title":"","content":"If it transforms clothing, then why not guns, swords, or even the car you are sitting in? Perhaps it's anything in contact with the users flesh?<br /> Then what happens if you're touching an opponent, do <i>their</i> clothes and/or weapons get affected because you're touching them? If not, then how would the Discipline determine possession for the purposes of which pieces of cloth, stone, leather, plastic, or metal to transform?<br /> How many degrees of separation are allowed? Does the wallet in your pocket transform or is it just the pants touching your skin? How about the credit cards in the wallet?<br /> <br /> If the ST wants to gloss over the &quot;you're naked, what do you do now?&quot; part for fun, expediency, or whatever else, then that's their individual call but it's only the users body as written, and that's the only way it would make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 06-23-2016, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:14:03-07:00","id":919690,"title":"","content":"The reason to use word Flesh over Body or Person is very simple and has nothing to do with intention of destroying clothes. It's the fact that word &quot;flesh&quot; is very fleshy, very visceral, full of blood and meat and bone, while body, person are relatively neutral and lack the wet, twitching and pulsing aroma of &quot;twisting flesh&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-23-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T08:24:30-07:00","id":919722,"title":"","content":"Clothes not changing with the werewolf make some sense because losing control and waking up bloodied and naked in an unknown place is a classic trope of werewolf stories.<br /> <br /> The same almost never happens in vampire stories - hence, it makes no sense for it to happen with Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:06:53-07:00","id":919750,"title":"","content":"I play my character as removing her clothes before or needing to replace or recover them after transformation in most cases as common sense dictates. I don't think it's coincidence that Protean is a clan specific power of the clan designated as closest to the Beast and they tend to favor embracing the types of people who don't spend overmuch time worried about clothes. Especially when they are more than capable of taking them from the next person they come across anyway.<br /> I did see one ST who allowed the clothes to transtorm with the user for full body changes, but the items lost at least one durability each time and were affected by the environment so it was still possible that your clothes got ruined when you do stuff like melding into dirt for hours or the filthy water at the bottom of a sewage drain pipe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:02:21-07:00","id":919781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=919644#post919644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it transforms clothing, then why not guns, swords, or even the car you are sitting in? Perhaps it's anything in contact with the users flesh?<br /> Then what happens if you're touching an opponent, do <i>their</i> clothes and/or weapons get affected because you're touching them? If not, then how would the Discipline determine possession for the purposes of which pieces of cloth, stone, leather, plastic, or metal to transform?<br /> How many degrees of separation are allowed? Does the wallet in your pocket transform or is it just the pants touching your skin? How about the credit cards in the wallet?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It transforms you and whatever you're carrying. If you're in a car you can't be touching the earth, can you? *itsmagiciaintgottaexplainshit.jpg*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T11:08:28-07:00","id":919820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=919781#post919781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*itsmagiciaintgottaexplainshit.jpg*</div> </div> </div> </div>Not precisely accurate. A single Ordo Dracul Gangrel with a curious mind and an Obsession (Understand Protean) Condition can easily make a series of very simple tests to probe the observable limits, and then devise hypothesis and try even more testing to gain a scary amount of knowledge about protean (from an out of character perspective, specifically the storyteller's interpretations and ruling on the results of those test).<br /> <br /> Both custom and common Protean based Devotions can easily result.<br /> <br /> #ApplyingScientificMethodInCharacterWithinAGame<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-23-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:10:13-07:00","id":919853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=919781#post919781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It transforms you and whatever you're carrying. If you're in a car you can't be touching the earth, can you? *itsmagiciaintgottaexplainshit.jpg*</div> </div> </div> </div>Touching the earth? Sure, 3 or 4 degrees of separation which is the same logic for having your wallet and credit cards transform. Not to mention one can easily touch the ground while sitting in a car, though would it count if you're wearing socks and/or shoes?<br /> Also, define carrying. Is it things in your pockets? In your hands? I'm holding the steering wheel so does that count as the whole car or just the steering wheel? What if I stuff a seatbelt into my pocket?<br /> <br /> Things quickly reach the realm of absurdity (beyond the totally mundane act of being a vampire) very quickly when you include things that are not ones own bodily tissue.<br /> <br /> As some have mentioned above, this is fertile ground for Devotions and Ordo Scales as well as stories exploring the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 06-23-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:50:27-07:00","id":919984,"title":"","content":"I'd say that clothes and stuff in your pockets shift with you unless you'd rather it blow your clothes off, because some people might want that . If a player wants to try to rules laywer more into shifting with them I'd turn them down on the basis that Protean is a shapeshifitng power and not a hammerspace storage power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:10:46-07:00","id":920164,"title":"","content":"The first power of Protean melds a vampire with material. The vampire no longer bodily exists which is why damage is caused not by digging out the vampire but damaging the structure of the patch of dirt or concrete foundation, etc.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Protean works like Captain Marvel. Billy Batson says &quot;SHAZAM!&quot; and he disappears to be replaced with Captain Marvel, minus the bolt of lightning. Thematically, the change is more like a physical morphing from one form to another. This leads to two reasonable explanations regarding personal possessions in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Protean could not directly affect personal possessions so hand held objects may be dropped or clothing damaged. This would be annoying. I doubt it is the assumed position for this reason.<br /> <br /> The alternative is that Protean does affect objects worn that are meant to be worn and hand held objects held in the hand while the vampire is affected by Protean. When the power ends the affect of the personal possessions does as well and they too revert back. Sometimes they might temporarily disappear or clothing might rip but all is as it was when the power is over. It is magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T03:40:14-07:00","id":920277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=919853#post919853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touching the earth? Sure, 3 or 4 degrees of separation which is the same logic for having your wallet and credit cards transform. Not to mention one can easily touch the ground while sitting in a car, though would it count if you're wearing socks and/or shoes?<br /> Also, define carrying. Is it things in your pockets? In your hands? I'm holding the steering wheel so does that count as the whole car or just the steering wheel? What if I stuff a seatbelt into my pocket?<br /> <br /> Things quickly reach the realm of absurdity (beyond the totally mundane act of being a vampire) very quickly when you include things that are not ones own bodily tissue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything can be made absurd if you try really hard, and man, you're really giving it your best shot here.<br /> <br /> Ever since I've gotten into Vampire in 2003, I've been running with Protean transforming the user's belongings. You know how many times this caused an argument at the table throughout all this time? Zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As some have mentioned above, this is fertile ground for Devotions and Ordo Scales as well as stories exploring the concept. </div> </div> </div>Dealing with clothes when transforming isn't a story, it's a nuisance, that's why they even mitigated it in Werewolf 2e (where, unlike in Vampire, there are solid precedents in the source material for this interpretation). This isn't fertile ground for new powers - it's putting an annoying limitation on a power that works perfectly by itself, and forcing them to pay extra to avoid the resulting annoyance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T06:38:34-07:00","id":920330,"title":"","content":"What they did in werewolf is actually really clever. They made it so that in the situations where you'd expect the whole clothes ripping and waking up naked trope to play out, it does. Things like the First Change and unstable werewolves that try to deny what they are only to go berserk under the full moon and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:53:41-07:00","id":920371,"title":"","content":"Semantics is super important in these games. Like WHW said. it states flesh changes. Like I stated and Rathamus backed up it creates a slippery slope if we look at it as a vampire controlling materials. Protean is a very bestial power, natural and down to earth. Back in 2000 something when 1E was written protean specifically stated clothes. Now, with the current book protean has been completely revamped and 3/5 of them specifically state flesh. The 5th one says you become nothing more than smoke and hunger ... no longer does it state clothes. Besides what happens to your cellphone once it dematerializes into smoke??<br /> <br /> Anyway that said....<br /> <br /> What this thread has come up with is: Half think that clothes do not shift and gave actual evidence from the book to support their reasons. The other half seems to take on the stance, It is too inconvenient or DMmagic: Clothes shift.<br /> <br /> So let's say this Question is answered with: It is entirely up to the Story Teller and how they interpret the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:40:29-07:00","id":920418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920371#post920371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantics is super important in these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must respectfully but emphatically disagree. <i>Interpretation</i> is super important in these games because the rules are written in natural language instead of technical language. A certain subset of the fanbase tries to interpret the rules as though they were written in technical language, and for those fans, semantics <i>become</i> very important. But semantics are not <i>inherently</i> important. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920371#post920371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like WHW said. it states flesh changes. Like I stated and Rathamus backed up it creates a slippery slope if we look at it as a vampire controlling materials. Protean is a very bestial power, natural and down to earth. Back in 2000 something when 1E was written protean specifically stated clothes. Now, with the current book protean has been completely revamped and 3/5 of them specifically state flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the &quot;flesh&quot; verbiage was just chosen because it's evocative. 2e takes tone and style very seriously in its writing, and (for better or worse) occasionally makes assumptions about the audience's preexisting knowledge from 1e. Also, the slippery slope argument falls flat with a little application of common sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920371#post920371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 5th one says you become nothing more than smoke and hunger ... no longer does it state clothes. Besides what happens to your cellphone once it dematerializes into smoke??</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that, it dematerializes into smoke. Then when you re-materialize into a corpse, it re-materializes into a cell phone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920371#post920371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway that said....<br /> <br /> What this thread has come up with is: Half think that clothes do not shift and gave actual evidence from the book to support their reasons. The other half seems to take on the stance, It is too inconvenient or DMmagic: Clothes shift.<br /> <br /> So let's say this Question is answered with: It is entirely up to the Story Teller and how they interpret the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> so eloquently put it, If there's two or more ways to read the rules, the way(s) that make for better rules trump the way(s) that are the most technically correct. Now, which of these two interpretations makes for better rules depends on the game, but <i>that</i> should be the deciding factor, not semantics and slippery slope arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:40:04-07:00","id":920535,"title":"","content":"I was gonna write pretty much exactly what Charlaquin had written, so instead I'll just say I agree 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T18:14:55-07:00","id":920675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920277#post920277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever since I've gotten into Vampire in 2003, I've been running with Protean transforming the user's belongings. You know how many times this caused an argument at the table throughout all this time? Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not, because there is no drawback to using the power and no real decision making or planning required. Superheroes at night comes to mind and players tend to not complain about things like that. I am of the mind that drawbacks make a power more interesting, unless &quot;My wishes become reality&quot; is the most fun power ever?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920277#post920277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dealing with clothes when transforming isn't a story, it's a nuisance...</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you want to shift to a bat and fly to the top of the tower, bypassing all the neat things I have in place for you and the coterie to explore on the way up? OK but all your gear stays here, save whatever your batform can carry.<br /> About to die? Shift to smoke, who wouldn't, but you're trading your favorite gear for your life. Wanna try getting it back later?<br /> Crap, that Nos just disappeared, is it worth shifting to dogform to scent track him, or should I get this rare loot back to the Prince instead?<br /> You're going into a big battle. Do you gear up for the big fight or travel light in case you have to tuck and run? How highly do you estimate your chances of winning?<br /> Dawn is approaching, wanna try finding a hidey--hole for your stuff or is it better to live instead?<br /> Do you come back for your stuff later? Do you ask a coterie member to hold/carry it and impede their own function? Do you have to catch up later and split the party now? etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Gangrel clan in general is stereotypically geared toward a down to earth, primal experience. Personal possessions are a very human concept while animals have absolutely no concept of such things, save what they're <i>eating </i>right this very moment. I think having their signature power inherently making personal possessions more of a fleeting thing reinforces this concept of the Gangrel as being nudged away from civilization and Humanity by his very nature. It also imposes a bit of the Gangrel curse on others who wish to dabble in their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 06-24-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T18:19:09-07:00","id":920678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920418#post920418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must respectfully but emphatically disagree. <i>Interpretation</i> is super important in these games because the rules are written in natural language instead of technical language. A certain subset of the fanbase tries to interpret the rules as though they were written in technical language, and for those fans, semantics <i>become</i> very important. But semantics are not <i>inherently</i> important.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think the &quot;flesh&quot; verbiage was just chosen because it's evocative. 2e takes tone and style very seriously in its writing, and (for better or worse) occasionally makes assumptions about the audience's preexisting knowledge from 1e. Also, the slippery slope argument falls flat with a little application of common sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> Exactly that, it dematerializes into smoke. Then when you re-materialize into a corpse, it re-materializes into a cell phone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Agreed. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> so eloquently put it, If there's two or more ways to read the rules, the way(s) that make for better rules trump the way(s) that are the most technically correct. Now, which of these two interpretations makes for better rules depends on the game, but <i>that</i> should be the deciding factor, not semantics and slippery slope arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never said interpretation was not important. We interpret things by the words chosen. The words chosen have different connotations, which leads to the interpretations. It's a circle Semantics and Interpretation go hand in hand. Like you said 2E takes it's tone and style. It chose it's words carefully. Two people can read the same thing and come away with two different stories. It's just how we associate the words to the meanings and that is perfectly fine. <br /> <br /> We are both on the same page with Heavy arms though when it comes down to it. --- &gt; Do what is best for the game or what the Story teller says. I don't think it's worth fighting over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T18:24:31-07:00","id":920683,"title":"","content":"I don't think we're fighting, we seem to be in agreement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T14:59:44-07:00","id":921182,"title":"","content":"When the rules are ambiguous, it is always up to the ST to interpret and make up a rule as the person sees fit. Why should the text force someone to play a certain way? I think that is where the ambiguity came from. We can only determine the options and the consequences of each. People have to make the decision on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:23:37-07:00","id":921655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=920675#post920675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course not, because there is no drawback to using the power and no real decision making or planning required. Superheroes at night comes to mind and players tend to not complain about things like that. I am of the mind that drawbacks make a power more interesting, unless &quot;My wishes become reality&quot; is the most fun power ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Protean already has a drawback - it's called being a vampire.<br /> 2. You're shifting goalposts here. You claimed the power is absurd and impossible to adjudicate on the fly. If it were, I'd have had arguments at my table, including ones started by me if I ever felt the power was abused. It wasn't, because people are good at instinctively grasping simple concepts like &quot;you and whatever you have on yourself&quot;. What's subjectively interesting to either of us has no bearing on the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you sure you want to shift to a bat and fly to the top of the tower, bypassing all the neat things I have in place for you and the coterie to explore on the way up? OK but all your gear stays here, save whatever your batform can carry.<br /> About to die? Shift to smoke, who wouldn't, but you're trading your favorite gear for your life. Wanna try getting it back later?<br /> Crap, that Nos just disappeared, is it worth shifting to dogform to scent track him, or should I get this rare loot back to the Prince instead?<br /> You're going into a big battle. Do you gear up for the big fight or travel light in case you have to tuck and run? How highly do you estimate your chances of winning?<br /> Dawn is approaching, wanna try finding a hidey--hole for your stuff or is it better to live instead?<br /> Do you come back for your stuff later? Do you ask a coterie member to hold/carry it and impede their own function? Do you have to catch up later and split the party now? etc. etc. </div> </div> </div>Circumventing obstacles and avoiding harm is what Protean is supposed to do. You're not making things more interesting by piling these complications on it - you're punishing the player for trying to use their character's powers in situations they're intended to be used in, and possibly forcing him into participating in scenes he specifically paid experience to avoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gangrel clan in general is stereotypically geared toward a down to earth, primal experience. Personal possessions are a very human concept while animals have absolutely no concept of such things, save what they're <i>eating </i>right this very moment. I think having their signature power inherently making personal possessions more of a fleeting thing reinforces this concept of the Gangrel as being nudged away from civilization and Humanity by his very nature. It also imposes a bit of the Gangrel curse on others who wish to dabble in their powers. </div> </div> </div>Right, 'cause everyone loves ham-handed attempts at forcing their character into the clan stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:38:10-07:00","id":924023,"title":"","content":"The way I take it is the same way <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/madrox/4005-7910/\" target=\"_blank\">Multiple Man's</a> duplication power works; his clothing and relatively small items he is carrying get copied. Living/organic matter cannot be duplicated (besides himself of course), complex devices cannot be duplicated (and if they do, they are mangled/malfunctioning dupes that break down easily). Simple objects like a baseball bat, a knife, money, etc. can be duped, but the copied money might have some inconsistencies between each other.<br /> <br /> So using Jamie as a model for how Protean works, objects (besides the clothing) that shapeshift with the vampire must be smaller than, say, a football, and no more complex than a knife or photograph/money. Something like a gun might not be able to shift with you since it has complex moving parts, and in some cases would be too large. Obviously under this model we can't have a vampire melding into bank vaults and such, <i>although</i> there are tales of vampires able to walk through solid matter. It could be a willpower or merit or some later evolution of the power of Protean that allows you to do something like that. Neat idea if you ask me, but it would not allow for a total meld perhaps. Also, I recall something in VtM that allowed for a vampire to meld with stone/concrete, so they were able to make a building their little haven for the day, so there's that too.<br /> <br /> Basically that means you're gonna need to stay in human form if you're carrying a usb stick or memory chip with vital information on it, lest you drop it in favor of saving your own hide. This allows for some of those plot hooks Rathamus mentioned (whoops, dropped your uzi/sword/cellphone/large painting you were stealing/data disc, but at least you're safe) but avoids the issues of &quot;lolz, naked vampire running around&quot; and even allows you to keep a few personal (small) items with you, either of sentimental value or actual use, like your knuckle-duster, bowie knife, or driver's license.<br /> <br /> As one extra point, let's not forget the countless vampire stories where the vampire (usually Dracula) shapeshifted not only himself into a tiny bat/large wolf/glowing mist, but also his attire for that evening, including the ever classy cape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7234,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","user":"The Dreamweaver","date":". 06-30-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:17:20-07:00","id":924517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918701-rules-vampire-the-requiem-second-edition-protean-vs-clothing?p=921655#post921655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're shifting goalposts here.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sake of discussion please allow me plant the &quot;goalpost&quot;* here:<br /> <br /> I think we can agree that there is room for interpretation in the Rules As Written (and I especially like the wording as is), and there is a spectrum of interesting &quot;if this, then that&quot; consequences for the stories based on those different interpretations. I think a good goalpost for this thread would be catalog the different interpretations and their good/neutral/bad consequences. It might also be useful to list themes and tropes supported by using different interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-01-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:25:47-07:00","id":929809,"title":"","content":"Protean preserves your clothing, because when I've fooled with having it the other way, it just introduces extra stuff to keep track of for no extra drama.<br /> <br /> Doesn't impact the setting or themes to do it the other way, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}